IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `acc-types`

-- Accident Compensation Act 2001 — GOALS 2 AND 4: CLAIMS AND DISPUTES.
--
--   Goal 2: "Was the claim lodged in time; by when must the Corporation
--            decide it; and if it misses that date, is cover deemed?"
--   Goal 4: "Is a review application in time and admissible; when must the
--            review be decided, and when is a decision deemed; when is an
--            appeal or a further appeal due?"
--
-- Source: ../source/ACC2001.txt — Part 3 (ss 39-66) and Part 5 (ss 133-164).

§ `Goal 2 — claims and decisions`

-- s 53(3): a claim "within 12 months after the date on which he or she
-- suffers the personal injury", or for an entitlement within 12 months after
-- the need arose; (4) for a treatment injury, 12 months after the later of the
-- date a registered health professional first considered it a treatment
-- injury and the date it was suffered. (2): a late claim must not be
-- declined for lateness "unless the claim's lateness prejudices the
-- Corporation".
@ref s 53(3)-(4)
GIVEN `injury or need on` IS A DATE, `first considered a treatment injury on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`a claim is due by, injury or need` `injury or need on` `, treatment injury recognised` `first considered a treatment injury on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `first considered a treatment injury on`
    WHEN JUST r  THEN `add months` (`the later of` r `injury or need on`) 12
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` `injury or need on` 12

@ref s 53(2)
GIVEN `lodged on` IS A DATE, due IS A DATE, `lateness prejudices the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may decline for lateness, lodged` `lodged on` `, due` due `, prejudiced:` `lateness prejudices the Corporation` IF
    `lodged on` GREATER THAN due AND `lateness prejudices the Corporation`

-- s 57(1): complicated claims — mental injury under s 21 or 21B, work-related
-- gradual process, treatment injury, or a claim lodged late.
@ref s 57(1)
GIVEN `mental injury under s 21 or 21B` IS A BOOLEAN, `work gradual process` IS A BOOLEAN, `treatment injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `lodged late` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a complicated claim, mental:` `mental injury under s 21 or 21B` `, gradual process:` `work gradual process` `, treatment:` `treatment injury` `, late:` `lodged late` IF
    `mental injury under s 21 or 21B` OR `work gradual process` OR `treatment injury` OR `lodged late`

-- s 56(2), (5): an ordinary claim decided "no later than 21 days" after
-- lodging, or, with an extension for more information, "within 4 months".
-- s 57(2)-(4): a complicated claim within 2 months, an extension "must not
-- exceed 2 months", and with agreed further extensions "within 9 months".
@ref ss 56(2), (5), 57(2)-(4)
GIVEN lodged IS A DATE, complicated IS A BOOLEAN, `extended for information` IS A BOOLEAN, `further extensions agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the claim must be decided by, lodged` lodged `, complicated:` complicated `, extended:` `extended for information` `, further extensions:` `further extensions agreed` MEANS
    IF complicated
    THEN BRANCH IF `further extensions agreed` THEN `add months` lodged 9
                IF `extended for information`  THEN `add months` lodged 4
                OTHERWISE                          `add months` lodged 2
    ELSE IF `extended for information` THEN `add months` lodged 4 ELSE lodged PLUS 21

-- s 58(1): if the Corporation "fails to comply with a time limit under section
-- 56 or section 57", the claimant "is to be regarded as having a decision ...
-- that he or she has cover"; (2)(c) dated the expiry of the time limit.
@ref s 58
GIVEN `decided on` IS A MAYBE DATE, due IS A DATE, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cover is deemed, decided` `decided on` `, due` due `, as at` `as at` IF
    CONSIDER `decided on`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d GREATER THAN due
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `as at` GREATER THAN due

-- s 65(2): a deemed decision may be revised, but payments before revision are
-- not recoverable unless the claimant was "intentionally misleading".
@ref s 65(2)
GIVEN `the claimant was intentionally misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `payments under a deemed cover decision may be recovered, misleading:` `the claimant was intentionally misleading` IF
    `the claimant was intentionally misleading`

-- s 66: claim files kept "for at least 10 years after the date of the latest
-- action". s 75: whether a rehabilitation plan is needed is decided "within
-- 13 weeks after the Corporation accepts" cover.
@ref s 66
GIVEN `latest action` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the claim file must be kept until, latest action` `latest action` MEANS `add years` `latest action` 10

@ref s 75
GIVEN accepted IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the need for a rehabilitation plan must be decided by, cover accepted` accepted MEANS accepted PLUS 91

§ `Goal 4 — reviews and appeals`

-- s 135(2)(f): a review "within 3 months" of the decision (or notice);
-- (2)(g): for an entitlement claim, "not ... less than 21 days after the date
-- the claim for entitlement is made". (3): a late application must be
-- accepted for extenuating circumstances. s 134(1A): no review of a s 68(3)
-- discretion.
@ref s 135(2)(f)-(g), (3)
GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE, `applied on` IS A DATE, `entitlement claimed on` IS A MAYBE DATE, `extenuating circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the review application is in time, notified` `notified on` `, applied` `applied on` `, entitlement claimed` `entitlement claimed on` `, extenuating:` `extenuating circumstances` IF
        (`applied on` AT MOST `add months` `notified on` 3 OR `extenuating circumstances`)
    AND `not premature`
    WHERE
        `not premature` MEANS
            CONSIDER `entitlement claimed on`
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `applied on` AT LEAST (c PLUS 21) OR `extenuating circumstances`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 141(3): notice of the hearing "at least 7 days before". s 144(1): the
-- decision "within 28 days after" the hearing finishes. s 146: a deemed
-- decision for the applicant if no hearing date is "set within 3 months
-- after the review application is received" and the applicant did not cause
-- the delay; dated 3 months after receipt.
@ref s 141(3)
GIVEN hearing IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`notice of the review hearing is due by, hearing` hearing MEANS hearing MINUS 7

@ref s 144(1)
GIVEN `hearing finished` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the review decision is due by, hearing finished` `hearing finished` MEANS `hearing finished` PLUS 28

@ref s 146
GIVEN received IS A DATE, `hearing date set on` IS A MAYBE DATE, `the applicant caused or contributed to the delay` IS A BOOLEAN, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a review decision is deemed for the applicant, received` received `, hearing set` `hearing date set on` `, applicant delayed:` `the applicant caused or contributed to the delay` `, as at` `as at` IF
        (NOT `the applicant caused or contributed to the delay`)
    AND `as at` AT LEAST `add months` received 3
    AND CONSIDER `hearing date set on`
        WHEN JUST s  THEN s GREATER THAN `add months` received 3
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 148(2): costs "must" be awarded if the decision is fully or partly for
-- the applicant; "may" if not but the applicant acted reasonably; (3) the
-- same if the Corporation revises its decision in the applicant's favour
-- before the hearing; (5) payable "within 28 days".
@ref s 148(2)-(3)
GIVEN `for the applicant, fully or partly` IS A BOOLEAN, `revised for the applicant before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `review costs must be awarded, for applicant:` `for the applicant, fully or partly` `, revised before hearing:` `revised for the applicant before the hearing` IF
    `for the applicant, fully or partly` OR `revised for the applicant before the hearing`

@ref s 148(5)
GIVEN awarded IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`review costs must be paid by, awarded` awarded MEANS awarded PLUS 28

-- s 151(3): the notice of appeal "within 28 days after the date on which the
-- reviewer gives a copy of the review decision", or after the deemed decision
-- date, or later if the District Court allows.
@ref s 151(3)
GIVEN `decision given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the appeal must be filed by, review decision given` `decision given` MEANS `decision given` PLUS 28

-- s 149(3): no appeal against a review decision on a Code complaint. (4): an
-- employer may appeal only a decision that an injury is work-related.
@ref s 149
GIVEN `a Code complaint review` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appellant is the employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `about whether the injury is work-related` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies to the District Court, Code complaint:` `a Code complaint review` `, employer:` `the appellant is the employer` `, work-related question:` `about whether the injury is work-related` IF
    (NOT `a Code complaint review`) AND ((NOT `the appellant is the employer`) OR `about whether the injury is work-related`)

-- s 162(2), (4): leave to appeal to the High Court "within 21 days after the
-- District Court's decision", and special leave within 21 days after refusal.
@ref s 162(2), (4)
GIVEN `decided or refused` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`leave to appeal must be sought by, decided or refused` `decided or refused` MEANS `decided or refused` PLUS 21

-- s 152(3): the Corporation gives the Registrar the names "within 7 days".
@ref s 152(3)
GIVEN requested IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Corporation must give the Registrar the names by, requested` requested MEANS requested PLUS 7

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 39-52, 54, 55, 59-64, 65(1), (3)-(5), 133, 134, 136-140, 142, 143, 145, 147, 150, 153-161, 163, 164
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`claims and disputes provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 39-47: the Code of ACC Claimants' Rights — purpose, preparation, consultation, approval, obligations, amendment"
         "ss 48-52, 54, 55: lodging claims, providers lodging, the Corporation's responsibilities, manner of claiming, reasonable timely decisions, claimant's duties"
         "ss 59-64: cover decided by the Act, not by levies; Schedule 2 injuries; hearing loss tests; clinical advice; review rights; written reasons"
         "s 65(1), (3)-(5): revision of decisions in error"
         "ss 133, 134: decisions stay in effect pending review; who may apply"
         "ss 136-140, 142, 143, 145, 147: acknowledgement, independent reviewers, conduct, who may be heard, records kept 2 years, the decision's substance and effect"
         "ss 150, 153-161, 163, 164: appeal procedure, hearing, evidence, assessors, privacy orders, decisions, the Court of Appeal, costs of appeals"
